## Summary

I have successfully identified and fixed the bug in the `normalizeUrl` function in `src/url_utils.ts`.

### The Problem
The original code had a `break;` statement inside the loop that processes tracking parameters. This caused the loop to exit after removing only the first matching tracking parameter instead of all of them.

### The Fix Applied
I removed the `break;` statement on line 14 in `/Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmpppffqkn1/run/src/url_utils.ts`, allowing the loop to continue processing all tracking parameters and remove them all rather than stopping after just the first one.

### Verification
I conducted thorough testing to confirm the fix works correctly:
- URLs with multiple tracking parameters (like `utm_source` and `fbclid`) now have ALL tracking parameters stripped
- URLs with single tracking parameters still work correctly  
- URLs with no tracking parameters remain unchanged
- URLs with tracking parameters plus other parameters properly preserve the non-tracking parameters

The fix ensures that every tracking parameter in `TRACKING_PARAMS` that's present in a URL will be removed, not just the first one found. This resolves the bug where only one of multiple tracking parameters was being stripped from bookmarked URLs.

The verification using direct JavaScript execution confirms that URLs with multiple tracking parameters are now properly normalized to remove all tracking parameters as intended.

